# Protected paths — enforced by .claude/hooks/protected-paths-gate.sh on every Edit/Write.
#
# One glob per line. Everything after `#` is the REASON and the ROUTE — it is shown verbatim
# when the gate blocks, so write it for the person who just hit the wall:
#     <glob>    # <why this is protected> — <what to do instead>
#
# Globs: `*` matches within a path segment, `**` matches across segments, `?` one character.
# Paths are matched relative to the repo root. Blank lines and comment-only lines are ignored.
# This is the deterministic layer behind the "never edit generated files" rules
# (api-contracts.md, ddd.md). Add a line when a path is frozen or generated; remove it when it
# is not. Changes to this file are reviewed like code.

server/node_modules/**                # committed third-party deps (5k+ tracked files) — change server/package.json and run npm install in server/ as a deliberate, reviewed change
**/gen/**                             # generated code — change the generator or its input, then regenerate
**/*.generated.*                      # generated code — change the source it is generated from
**/node_modules/**                    # dependencies — change package.json and reinstall
docs/glossary.md                      # generated by /knowledge-update — edit the domain model, then regenerate
docs/feature-index.yaml               # generated by /features — regenerate, do not hand-edit
docs/change-impact-matrix.md          # generated by /knowledge-update
# Examples — uncomment and adapt:
# src/legacy/v1/**                    # frozen package — new work goes in v2/ (ADR-NNN)
# db/migrations/**                    # migrations need a change ticket — use /scaffold --migrate, which claims a sequence number in MIGRATIONS-LOG.md
